; Network-Startup: the network brought up behind the boot. The
; Startup-Sequence runs it in a shell of its own, so the boot waits for
; none of it.

; A board without an interface's device, or a network nobody answers
; on, stops nothing here.
FailAt 21

; Every interface in DEVS:NetInterfaces/, and a DHCP address waited for:
; ten seconds at the most.
C:net/AddNetInterface ALL QUIET

; The clock set from a time server: DHCP's, ENVARC:Sys/net/timeserver's,
; or pool.ntp.org, in the local time of ENVARC:Sys/timezone.
C:net/TimeSync QUIET
